  "whole_exchange_context": "A brusque town-square shopkeeper stops Lil and asks whether she knows the Crusades. The original two answers are 知っている and 知らない. The two corresponding source explanations differ:one challenges the favorable account the listener is assumed to know;the other reports how Europe supposedly describes the Crusaders. Both converge on the shopkeeper's bitter accusation that the received chivalric Holy-Land story is a convenient lie and locals know better. Lil asks what he means. Actor17 cites reports that wealth was the real objective and that plunder and slaughter were unrestricted. The shopkeeper condemns convenient rewritten history and declares their real hero to be Saladin. Lil asks who that is;actor17 explains the figure's place in Islamic history and praises humane fighting,treatment of prisoners/people and peace terms. Lil admires strength joined with good character. Actor17 then remembers hearing that Saladin's armor is missing and suggests looking for it if she wants to follow his example. Preserve the progression from brusque challenge through regional resentment to explanation,admiration and an uncertain armor lead. Historical/religious assertions remain the characters' reported claims and viewpoints;do not import outside history or correct the source from another retelling. Neither choice routing,natural event eligibility nor complete item effects are yet proven. Exact source name fields separate real name components from unused role-location metadata. Actor85 shares clean広場の店主 with the existing actor82 wider label lead;this is an additional source reference,not a closed global native/shared consumer census or an approval to append Islam/Europe as nationality. B222 has also been inventoried clean-only;its following conversation remains independently pending.",
